# Git and GitLab mutations (paramount)

These rules override convenience. When in doubt, ask the user.

## Personas / subagents

- **Must never** run `git commit`, `git push`, or any mutating GitLab action.
- Implement and propose; leave Finish shipping to the main orchestrator + user consent.

## Main orchestrator (this chat when running `/run` or Finish)

- **Never** silently auto-push, auto-create/open an MR, or call mutating GitLab APIs — except the `/rebase` push below.
- **Commit:** may `git add` / `git commit` **only** when the user explicitly selects an orchestrator-offered commit message (or equivalent explicit intent). If they choose "do not commit" / "other-manual", do not commit.
- **Push:** may `git push` (including `--force-with-lease` when a confirmed rewrite requires it) only after an explicit user **Yes** to a push prompt.
- **Exception — `/rebase`:** invoking `/rebase` **is** that consent. After a clean rebase of a non-protected working branch, push with `git push --force-with-lease origin <working-branch>` (or `git push -u origin <working-branch>` when there is no upstream). Do **not** ask for a second Yes. Do **not** push on conflict, dirty-tree skip, failed pull, or when the current branch is the main/default. Never `--force` / `-f` without lease. Never push to `main` / `master` / `develop` / `development` / `release/*`.
- **Branch create/switch** and every mutating GitLab action (MR create/update, write API) require **explicit confirmation at that step**.
- After MR confirmation: create/update via **GitLab MCP** (`mcp__GitLab__*` / project GitLab tools), always presenting title/body for review first. Body: project skill `bcs-gitlab-mr-from-spec` + `scripts/tools/mr-description-from-spec.sh`. MR / mutating GitLab API remains **user-run** after that confirmation.
- **`glab` is not used** in this workspace (not authenticated) — do not suggest it.
- **`/rebase`** never creates/updates an MR via GitLab API and never transitions a Jira ticket. A git push of the rebased source branch is git-sync, not an MR API mutation.

## Hooks (defense in depth)

- `before-shell` blocks catastrophic deletes, destructive SQL, force-push to protected branches.
- `subagent-gate` (`preToolUse` Write) blocks writes into child repos on `main` / `master` / `develop` / `release/*`.
